Architecture plan

Project shape
- `web/src/components/graph/graph-canvas.tsx` owns Cytoscape integration, node/edge styling, interaction hooks, and the debug node-position feed used by Playwright.
- `web/src/App.tsx` owns the workspace state: current query text, `canvasGraph`, selected / inspected node ids, label-scan state, tab state, and the transforms that map API results into the canvas.
- `web/src/lib/api-types.ts` is the shared frontend contract for `GraphNode`, `GraphEdge`, `GraphResult`, `QueryResult`, and the graph-value type guards used when rebuilding canvas data from result rows.
- `web/tests/smoke.spec.ts` is the end-to-end contract for the intended canvas behavior and will be updated last so it validates the first two issues together.

Module / file plan
- Issue #83 should stay centered in `graph-canvas.tsx`: keep one long-lived Cytoscape core in a ref, update its elements when props change, and preserve the existing selection / debug hooks while moving layout + per-label coloring into data-driven Cytoscape state.
- Issue #84 should stay centered in `App.tsx` with small helpers: derive the visible canvas graph from `QueryResult.rows`, reset selection counters when the graph is cleared, and keep node-expansion merge behavior compatible with the new canvas graph shape from issue #83.
- Issue #85 should only touch `web/tests/smoke.spec.ts` unless a tiny test-only affordance is needed from `graph-canvas.tsx` debug output.

Issue dependencies
- #83 is the foundation. It defines the single-instance Cytoscape behavior and the `data.label` / color behavior that later tests will assert against.
- #84 depends on #83 because the rebuilt canvas graph has to target the new Cytoscape element update path rather than recreating multiple canvas assumptions.
- #85 depends on both #83 and #84 because the smoke flow needs the final graph rendering behavior, label-scan result shaping, and clear-selection reset semantics.

Key design decisions
- Treat `App.tsx` state as the source of truth and `GraphCanvas` as a renderer / interaction adapter around Cytoscape.
- Keep shared graph-shape logic in small frontend helpers rather than changing the backend contract; the issues describe presentation and client-state behavior, not API schema changes.
- Preserve the existing `graph-node-positions` debug output so Playwright can continue to assert rendered graph state without introducing new browser-only test APIs.
- Use deterministic per-label coloring from node labels, not per-node ids, so relation-query tests can verify multiple visible label colors from mixed-label results.
- When clearing the canvas or replacing it from a label scan, reset derived selection state in the same state transition so counts and inspector UI cannot drift from the visible graph.
